.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-fix 1  "fix " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-fix \- Apply the fixes a finding decides on its own, proving each one before it is written. Previews by default
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx fix\fR [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-write\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-rounds\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-plan\fR] [\fB\-\-markdown\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply the fixes a finding decides on its own, proving each one before it is written. Previews by default
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
relaxed, standard, strict or pristine
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-write\fR
Write the fixes. Without it nothing on disk changes
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-rounds\fR \fI<MAX_ROUNDS>\fR
One fix can make the next one possible, so fixing repeats until a round finds nothing. Overrides `[fix] max_rounds`
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit one JSON object per fixed file instead of the reader\*(Aqs preview
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR
Report the findings `fix` will not touch, with the span, the source, the metric and the named refactoring, for a person or an agent to act on
.TP
\fB\-\-markdown\fR
With \-\-plan, emit markdown a person can paste rather than a report to read
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads. Defaults to the machine\*(Aqs parallelism
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `rqx.yaml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Leave the mouse to the terminal. Capture takes drag\-select away from it, and not every emulator passes shift+drag through
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx fix                             show what would change
  rqx fix \-w                          write it
  rqx fix \-\-plan                      the edits as a list, not a diff
